[2026-03-14T19:49:23.608Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0123dxoKPnY8b8UYmiSxHsGx","type":"tool_result","content":"151:#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge not shown when no unread notifications\n155:#### Test: Sidebar renders team sections\n157:- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Team Section\" with each team name as a collapsible section header. Under each team: \"Issues\" (list icon), \"Active Cycle\" (refresh-cw icon), \"Projects\" (folder icon), \"Views\" (layout icon).\n159:#### Test: Sidebar team section is collapsible\n162:- **Expected**: The team section collapses, hiding Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, and Views sub-links. Clicking again expands it back.\n164:#### Test: Sidebar team section collapse toggles multiple times\n169:#### Test: Sidebar team Issues link navigates to team issues page\n174:#### Test: Sidebar team Active Cycle link navigates to cycles page\n176:- **Action**: User clicks \"Active Cycle\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n177:- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/team/eng-1/cycles`.\n179:#### Test: Sidebar team Projects link navigates to team projects\n184:#### Test: Sidebar team Views link navigates to saved views\n--\n268:#### Test: Sidebar collapse toggle works multiple times in sequence\n273:#### Test: Sidebar team sections visible in collapsed mode\n275:- **Expected**: Team navigation items are still accessible in icon-only mode (icons for Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, Views are visible and clickable).\n277:#### Test: Sidebar workspace section visible in collapsed mode\n283:#### Test: Pressing C opens create issue modal\n--\n830:#### Test: Sort by can be changed multiple times\n837:#### Test: Team filters toolbar renders with all filter options\n839:- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays filter controls: \"Status\", \"Priority\", \"Assignee\", \"Label\", \"Project\", and \"Cycle\" filters. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a dropdown.\n841:#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n846:#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n--\n881:#### Test: Project filter dropdown shows all team projects\n886:#### Test: Project filter filters issues by selected projects\n891:#### Test: Cycle filter dropdown shows team cycles\n892:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has cycles \"Sprint 1\" (active), \"Sprint 2\" (upcoming)\n893:- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cycle\" filter button\n894:- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing \"Sprint 1\", \"Sprint 2\", and a \"No Cycle\" option. The active cycle is visually indicated. Each option has a checkbox.\n896:#### Test: Cycle filter filters issues by selected cycle\n897:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (in \"Sprint 1\"), ENG-2 (in \"Sprint 1\"), ENG-3 (no cycle)\n898:- **Action**: User opens Cycle filter and selects \"Sprint 1\"\n901:#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n906:#### Test: Clearing a filter restores all issues\n--\n1107:#### Test: Comment displays long text properly\n1114:#### Test: Sidebar renders all property fields\n1115:- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", assignee \"Alice\", labels [\"Bug\", \"Frontend\"], project \"Auth Rewrite\", cycle \"Sprint 3\", due date \"2026-04-01\"\n1116:- **Expected**: The right sidebar displays all property fields: Status showing \"In Progress\" with half-circle yellow icon, Priority showing \"High\" with orange arrow-up icon, Assignee showing \"Alice\" with avatar, Labels showing \"Bug\" and \"Frontend\" as colored badges, Project showing \"Auth Rewrite\", Cycle showing \"Sprint 3\", Due Date showing \"Apr 1, 2026\", Created timestamp (read-only), and Updated timestamp (read-only).\n1118:#### Test: Change status via sidebar dropdown\n1123:#### Test: Select new status in sidebar\n--\n1175:#### Test: Search and select project\n1180:#### Test: Remove project assignment\n1185:#### Test: Change cycle via dropdown\n1186:- **Initial state**: Issue belongs to team \"Engineering\" which has cycles \"Sprint 2\" (completed), \"Sprint 3\" (active), \"Sprint 4\" (upcoming). Issue has no cycle assigned.\n1187:- **Action**: User clicks the Cycle field in the sidebar\n1188:- **Expected**: A dropdown appears showing available cycles for the team: \"Sprint 2\", \"Sprint 3\", \"Sprint 4\" with their date ranges.\n1190:#### Test: Select cycle\n1191:- **Initial state**: The cycle dropdown is open\n1193:- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. Cycle updates to show \"Sprint 3\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n1195:#### Test: Change due date via date picker\n1200:#### Test: Select due date\n--\n1219:#### Test: Use assignee selector multiple times in sequence\n1230:#### Test: Create issue modal renders with all form fields\n1232:- **Expected**: Modal displays: Team selector dropdown, Title text input, Description text area, Status dropdown, Priority dropdown, Assignee searchable selector, Labels multi-select, Project searchable selector, Cycle dropdown, Due date picker, and Parent issue searchable selector. All fields are visible and properly labeled.\n1234:#### Test: Modal opens from New Issue button on team issues page","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014vB59L6L4pzEX8iMoSPVUx","session_id":"76da8815-73a4-4291-afeb-dab9c3288c7d","uuid":"7389cbc7-dace-4fa4-8fd7-aefa6fb73218"}
