[2026-03-14T19:49:48.507Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015sS5JF5SoaNH1G9VizGdBX","type":"tool_result","content":"   800→#### Test: Sort by dropdown shows all sorting options\n   801→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   802→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Sort by\" control\n   803→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing options: Priority, Created date, Updated date, Status. Each option is clickable.\n   804→\n   805→#### Test: Sort by Priority orders issues by priority level\n   806→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with mixed priorities within status groups\n   807→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   808→- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by priority: Urgent first, then High, Medium, Low, No Priority last.\n   809→\n   810→#### Test: Sort by Created date orders issues by creation time\n   811→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues created at different times\n   812→- **Action**: User selects \"Created date\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   813→- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by creation date (newest first).\n   814→\n   815→#### Test: Sort by Updated date orders issues by last update time\n   816→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues updated at different times\n   817→- **Action**: User selects \"Updated date\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   818→- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by last update time (most recently updated first).\n   819→\n   820→#### Test: Sort by Status orders issues by status progression\n   821→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, group by is set to \"None\" (flat list)\n   822→- **Action**: User selects \"Status\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   823→- **Expected**: Issues are ordered by status progression: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled.\n   824→\n   825→#### Test: Sort works correctly within groups\n   826→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, grouped by Status, \"In Progress\" group has 3 issues with different priorities\n   827→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from Sort by\n   828→- **Expected**: The 3 issues within the \"In Progress\" group are reordered by priority (Urgent first, No Priority last). Other groups are similarly sorted.\n   829→\n   830→#### Test: Sort by can be changed multiple times\n   831→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   832→- **Action**: User sorts by \"Priority\", then by \"Created date\", then by \"Updated date\"\n   833→- **Expected**: Each sort change correctly reorders issues within their groups. The sort control updates to reflect the current selection.\n   834→\n   835→### TeamFilters\n   836→\n   837→#### Test: Team filters toolbar renders with all filter options\n   838→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/team/eng-1/issues`\n   839→- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays filter controls: \"Status\", \"Priority\", \"Assignee\", \"Label\", \"Project\", and \"Cycle\" filters. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a dropdown.\n   840→\n   841→#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n   842→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   843→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n   844→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red). Each option has a checkbox.\n   845→\n   846→#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n   847→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in Backlog (3), In Progress (2), Done (1)\n   848→- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects only \"In Progress\"\n   849→- **Expected**: Only the \"In Progress\" group is displayed with its 2 issues. Backlog and Done groups are hidden. The Status filter button shows a visual indicator that a filter is active.\n   850→\n   851→#### Test: Priority filter dropdown shows all priorities with icons\n   852→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   853→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Priority\" filter button\n   854→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing: Urgent (alert-triangle, red), High (arrow-up, orange), Medium (minus, yellow), Low (arrow-down, blue), No Priority (dots-horizontal, gray). Each option has a checkbox.\n   855→\n   856→#### Test: Priority filter filters issues by selected priorities\n   857→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with priorities High (2), Medium (1), Low (1)\n   858→- **Action**: User opens Priority filter and selects \"High\"\n   859→- **Expected**: Only issues with High priority are displayed across all status groups. Issues with Medium and Low priority are hidden.\n   860→\n   861→#### Test: Assignee filter dropdown shows all team members\n   862→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team \"Engineering\" has members Alice, Bob, and Charlie\n   863→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Assignee\" filter button\n   864→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all team members with their avatars and names: Alice, Bob, Charlie, and an \"Unassigned\" option. Each option has a checkbox.\n   865→\n   866→#### Test: Assignee filter filters issues by selected assignees\n   867→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (Alice), ENG-2 (Bob), ENG-3 (Alice), ENG-4 (unassigned)\n   868→- **Action**: User opens Assignee filter and selects \"Alice\"\n   869→- **Expected**: Only issues assigned to Alice are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-3). Issues assigned to Bob and unassigned issues are hidden.\n   870→\n   871→#### Test: Label filter dropdown shows all available labels\n   872→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (green), \"Improvement\" (blue)\n   873→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" filter button\n   874→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all workspace labels with their colored dots and names. Each option has a checkbox.\n   875→\n   876→#### Test: Label filter filters issues by selected labels\n   877→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (labeled \"Bug\"), ENG-2 (labeled \"Feature\"), ENG-3 (labeled \"Bug\", \"Feature\")\n   878→- **Action**: User opens Label filter and selects \"Bug\"\n   879→- **Expected**: Only issues with the \"Bug\" label are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-3). ENG-2 is hidden.\n   880→\n   881→#### Test: Project filter dropdown shows all team projects\n   882→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has projects \"Auth Rewrite\" and \"Dashboard v2\"\n   883→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Project\" filter button\n   884→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing \"Auth Rewrite\", \"Dashboard v2\", and a \"No Project\" option. Each has a checkbox.\n   885→\n   886→#### Test: Project filter filters issues by selected projects\n   887→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (project \"Auth Rewrite\"), ENG-2 (project \"Dashboard v2\"), ENG-3 (no project)\n   888→- **Action**: User opens Project filter and selects \"Auth Rewrite\"\n   889→- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 is shown. ENG-2 and ENG-3 are hidden.\n   890→\n   891→#### Test: Cycle filter dropdown shows team cycles\n   892→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has cycles \"Sprint 1\" (active), \"Sprint 2\" (upcoming)\n   893→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cycle\" filter button\n   894→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing \"Sprint 1\", \"Sprint 2\", and a \"No Cycle\" option. The active cycle is visually indicated. Each option has a checkbox.\n   895→\n   896→#### Test: Cycle filter filters issues by selected cycle\n   897→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (in \"Sprint 1\"), ENG-2 (in \"Sprint 1\"), ENG-3 (no cycle)\n   898→- **Action**: User opens Cycle filter and selects \"Sprint 1\"\n   899→- **Expected**: Only issues in Sprint 1 are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-2). ENG-3 is hidden.\n   900→\n   901→#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n   902→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (High priority, Bug label, In Progress), ENG-2 (High priority, Feature label, In Progress), ENG-3 (Low priority, Bug label, Backlog)\n   903→- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter and \"Bug\" in Label filter\n   904→- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 is shown (matches both High priority AND Bug label). ENG-2 and ENG-3 are hidden.\n   905→\n   906→#### Test: Clearing a filter restores all issues\n   907→- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\" only, showing 2 issues out of 6 total\n   908→- **Action**: User opens Status filter and deselects \"In Progress\" (or clicks a \"Clear\" option)\n   909→- **Expected**: All 6 issues are shown again across all status groups, same as the unfiltered view.\n   910→\n   911→#### Test: Filter state shows active filter indicators\n   912→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no filters applied\n   913→- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter\n   914→- **Expected**: The Priority filter button shows a visual indicator that it is active (e.g., highlighted background, badge showing \"1\", or different styling). Other filter buttons remain in their default/inactive state.\n   915→\n   916→#### Test: Filters can be used repeatedly after clearing\n   917→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated with multiple issues at various statuses and priorities\n   918→- **Action**: User applies Priority filter for \"High\", clears it, then applies Assignee filter for \"Alice\", clears it, then applies Status filter for \"Done\"\n   919→- **Expected**: Each filter application and clearing works correctly. After the final action, only \"Done\" issues are shown. All filter controls remain responsive and functional through multiple interactions.\n   920→\n   921→#### Test: Filters work correctly with grouping options\n   922→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issues grouped by Priority, Assignee filter set to \"Alice\"\n   923→- **Expected**: Only Alice's issues are shown, grouped under their respective priority headers. Empty priority groups (where Alice has no issues) are not displayed.\n   924→\n   925→#### Test: Filters persist while navigating within the page\n   926→- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\", viewing filtered results\n   927→- **Action**: User clicks an issue title to view detail, then navigates back to `/team/eng-1/issues`\n   928→- **Expected**: The filters are still applied showing only \"In Progress\" issues. The filter state is preserved across navigation.\n   929→\n   930→#### Test: Assignee filter allows multi-select\n   931→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues assigned to Alice (2), Bob (1), Charlie (1)\n   932→- **Action**: User opens Assignee filter, checks \"Alice\" and \"Bob\"\n   933→- **Expected**: Issues assigned to Alice and Bob are shown. Charlie's issues are hidden. The filter button indicates 2 assignees selected.\n   934→\n   935→## Issue Detail Page (`/issue/:issueId`)\n   936→\n   937→**Components**: IssueHeader, IssueDescription, SubIssues, ActivityComments, IssueSidebar\n   938→\n   939→### IssueHeader\n   940→\n   941→#### Test: Issue header renders identifier and title\n   942→- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/issue/:issueId` for an existing issue with identifier \"ENG-42\" and title \"Fix login bug\"\n   943→- **Expected**: The header displays the issue identifier \"ENG-42\" and the title \"Fix login bug\" in large font. The identifier is non-editable. The status selector is visible below the title showing the current status with its icon and color.\n   944→\n   945→#### Test: Inline edit issue title\n   946→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for issue \"ENG-42\" with title \"Fix login bug\"\n   947→- **Action**: User clicks on the title text \"Fix login bug\"\n   948→- **Expected**: The title becomes an editable text input pre-filled with \"Fix login bug\". The input is focused and ready for editing.\n   949→\n   950→#### Test: Save edited issue title\n   951→- **Initial state**: User has clicked the title and it is in edit mode, showing \"Fix login bug\"\n   952→- **Action**: User clears the field, types \"Fix authentication bug\", and presses Enter (or clicks away to blur)\n   953→- **Expected**: The title updates to \"Fix authentication bug\". The change is persisted to the database. The title returns to display mode. An activity entry is created recording the title change.\n   954→\n   955→#### Test: Cancel title edit on Escape\n   956→- **Initial state**: User has clicked the title and it is in edit mode, showing \"Fix login bug\"\n   957→- **Action**: User types some characters, then presses Escape\n   958→- **Expected**: The title reverts to the original \"Fix login bug\" without saving. The field returns to display mode.\n   959→\n   960→#### Test: Title edit validates non-empty\n   961→- **Initial state**: User has clicked the title and it is in edit mode\n   962→- **Action**: User clears the title field completely and presses Enter\n   963→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown (e.g., red border or tooltip) indicating the title cannot be empty. The original title is preserved.\n   964→\n   965→#### Test: Inline status selector displays current status\n   966→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with status \"In Progress\"\n   967→- **Expected**: The status selector below the title shows a half-circle icon in yellow and the text \"In Progress\".\n   968→\n   969→#### Test: Change status via inline selector\n   970→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with status \"Todo\"\n   971→- **Action**: User clicks the status selector\n   972→- **Expected**: A dropdown appears showing all statuses (Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled) each with their respective icon and color.\n   973→\n   974→#### Test: Select new status from dropdown\n   975→- **Initial state**: The status dropdown is open, current status is \"Todo\"\n   976→- **Action**: User clicks \"In Progress\" in the dropdown\n   977→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The status selector updates to show the half-circle icon in yellow with text \"In Progress\". The change is persisted to the database. An activity entry is created recording the status change from \"Todo\" to \"In Progress\". A notification is created for subscribers of this issue.\n   978→\n   979→#### Test: Status dropdown closes on outside click\n   980→- **Initial state**: The status dropdown is open\n   981→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown\n   982→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the status.\n   983→\n   984→#### Test: Issue detail page shows correct layout with left and right panels\n   985→- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/issue/:issueId` for an existing issue\n   986→- **Expected**: The page displays a two-panel layout: the left panel (~70% width) contains the issue header, description, sub-issues, and activity/comments sections. The right panel (~30% width) contains the sidebar with issue properties.\n   987→\n   988→### IssueDescription\n   989→\n   990→#### Test: Description renders markdown content\n   991→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with a markdown description containing headings, bold text, code blocks, and bullet lists\n   992→- **Expected**: The description area renders the markdown as formatted HTML — headings are styled, bold text is bold, code blocks have monospace font with background, and bullet lists are properly indented.\n   993→\n   994→#### Test: Description shows placeholder when empty\n   995→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with no description\n   996→- **Expected**: The description area shows a placeholder text (e.g., \"Add a description...\") in muted/gray text, indicating it is clickable to add content.\n   997→\n   998→#### Test: Click to edit description\n   999→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page with a description \"This is a bug in the login flow\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014vB59L6L4pzEX8iMoSPVUx","session_id":"76da8815-73a4-4291-afeb-dab9c3288c7d","uuid":"07e69338-1bbb-4a38-b03f-e9666892ebe9"}
