[2026-03-14T19:49:48.535Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U9iGqx25c8zANxyao7jMKe","type":"tool_result","content":"  1200→#### Test: Select due date\n  1201→- **Initial state**: The date picker is open\n  1202→- **Action**: User selects April 15, 2026\n  1203→- **Expected**: The date picker closes. Due Date updates to show \"Apr 15, 2026\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1204→\n  1205→#### Test: Clear due date\n  1206→- **Initial state**: Issue has due date \"Apr 15, 2026\"\n  1207→- **Action**: User clicks the Due Date field and clicks a \"Clear\" or remove option\n  1208→- **Expected**: The due date is removed. The field shows as empty (e.g., \"No due date\"). The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1209→\n  1210→#### Test: Created and Updated timestamps are read-only\n  1211→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page. The issue was created on \"Mar 10, 2026\" and last updated \"Mar 14, 2026\".\n  1212→- **Expected**: The Created field shows \"Mar 10, 2026\" (or relative time like \"4 days ago\") and the Updated field shows \"Mar 14, 2026\" (or \"today\"). Both fields are not clickable/editable — they have no hover cursor change or click handler.\n  1213→\n  1214→#### Test: Sidebar dropdowns close on outside click\n  1215→- **Initial state**: The priority dropdown is open in the sidebar\n  1216→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown (e.g., on the description area)\n  1217→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the priority value.\n  1218→\n  1219→#### Test: Use assignee selector multiple times in sequence\n  1220→- **Initial state**: Issue is assigned to \"Alice\"\n  1221→- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee field, selects \"Bob\", then immediately clicks the Assignee field again and selects \"Charlie\"\n  1222→- **Expected**: The assignee correctly updates to \"Charlie\" after the second selection. Both changes create separate activity entries. The search input resets between uses.\n  1223→\n  1224→## Create Issue Modal\n  1225→\n  1226→**Components**: CreateIssueForm, CreateIssueActions\n  1227→\n  1228→### CreateIssueForm\n  1229→\n  1230→#### Test: Create issue modal renders with all form fields\n  1231→- **Initial state**: User is on Team Issues page for team \"Engineering\"\n  1232→- **Expected**: Modal displays: Team selector dropdown, Title text input, Description text area, Status dropdown, Priority dropdown, Assignee searchable selector, Labels multi-select, Project searchable selector, Cycle dropdown, Due date picker, and Parent issue searchable selector. All fields are visible and properly labeled.\n  1233→\n  1234→#### Test: Modal opens from New Issue button on team issues page\n  1235→- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/:teamId/issues` for team \"Engineering\"\n  1236→- **Action**: User clicks the \"New Issue\" button\n  1237→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens as an overlay. The Team selector is pre-selected to \"Engineering\". The Title input is focused.\n  1238→\n  1239→#### Test: Modal opens from keyboard shortcut C\n  1240→- **Initial state**: User is on `/my-issues`, no input fields are focused\n  1241→- **Action**: User presses \"C\" key\n  1242→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens as an overlay.\n  1243→\n  1244→#### Test: Team selector defaults to current team context\n  1245→- **Initial state**: User opens create issue modal from team \"Design\" issues page\n  1246→- **Expected**: The Team selector dropdown shows \"Design\" as the selected value.\n  1247→\n  1248→#### Test: Team selector allows changing team\n  1249→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" pre-selected. Teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\" exist.\n  1250→- **Action**: User clicks the Team selector dropdown and selects \"Design\"\n  1251→- **Expected**: Team selector now shows \"Design\". The Cycle dropdown updates to show \"Design\" team's cycles instead of \"Engineering\" team's cycles.\n  1252→\n  1253→#### Test: Title field is required\n  1254→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1255→- **Action**: User leaves the Title field empty and attempts to submit\n  1256→- **Expected**: A validation error appears indicating that title is required. The issue is not created.\n  1257→\n  1258→#### Test: Title field accepts text input\n  1259→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1260→- **Action**: User types \"Implement user authentication\" in the Title field\n  1261→- **Expected**: The Title field displays \"Implement user authentication\".\n  1262→\n  1263→#### Test: Description field supports markdown text entry\n  1264→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1265→- **Action**: User types \"## Overview\\nThis issue covers the auth flow\" in the Description text area\n  1266→- **Expected**: The Description field accepts and displays the markdown text.\n  1267→\n  1268→#### Test: Status dropdown defaults to Backlog\n  1269→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1270→- **Expected**: The Status dropdown shows \"Backlog\" with a dotted circle icon in gray as the default selected value.\n  1271→\n  1272→#### Test: Status dropdown shows all status options with icons\n  1273→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1274→- **Action**: User clicks the Status dropdown\n  1275→- **Expected**: Dropdown shows all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red).\n  1276→\n  1277→#### Test: Status dropdown allows selecting a different status\n  1278→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Status shows \"Backlog\"\n  1279→- **Action**: User clicks Status dropdown and selects \"Todo\"\n  1280→- **Expected**: Status dropdown now shows \"Todo\" with circle icon in gray.\n  1281→\n  1282→#### Test: Priority dropdown defaults to No Priority\n  1283→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1284→- **Expected**: The Priority dropdown shows \"No Priority\" with dots-horizontal icon in gray as the default value.\n  1285→\n  1286→#### Test: Priority dropdown shows all priority options with icons\n  1287→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1288→- **Action**: User clicks the Priority dropdown\n  1289→- **Expected**: Dropdown shows: Urgent (alert-triangle, red), High (arrow-up, orange), Medium (minus, yellow), Low (arrow-down, blue), No Priority (dots-horizontal, gray).\n  1290→\n  1291→#### Test: Priority dropdown allows selecting a priority\n  1292→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Priority shows \"No Priority\"\n  1293→- **Action**: User clicks Priority dropdown and selects \"High\"\n  1294→- **Expected**: Priority dropdown now shows \"High\" with arrow-up icon in orange.\n  1295→\n  1296→#### Test: Assignee selector is searchable\n  1297→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Workspace has members \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\", \"Carol Lee\".\n  1298→- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee selector and types \"Ali\"\n  1299→- **Expected**: The selector filters to show only \"Alice Smith\" with her avatar.\n  1300→\n  1301→#### Test: Assignee selector allows selecting a member\n  1302→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Assignee field is empty\n  1303→- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee selector, types \"Bob\", and clicks \"Bob Jones\"\n  1304→- **Expected**: Assignee field shows \"Bob Jones\" with his avatar.\n  1305→\n  1306→#### Test: Labels multi-select allows selecting multiple labels\n  1307→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Labels \"Bug\", \"Feature\", \"Improvement\" exist.\n  1308→- **Action**: User clicks Labels selector, selects \"Bug\", then selects \"Feature\"\n  1309→- **Expected**: Both \"Bug\" and \"Feature\" appear as colored badges in the Labels field.\n  1310→\n  1311→#### Test: Labels multi-select allows removing a selected label\n  1312→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with \"Bug\" and \"Feature\" labels selected\n  1313→- **Action**: User clicks the remove button on the \"Bug\" label badge\n  1314→- **Expected**: Only \"Feature\" remains selected in the Labels field.\n  1315→\n  1316→#### Test: Project selector is searchable\n  1317→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Projects \"API Redesign\", \"Mobile App\", \"Dashboard\" exist.\n  1318→- **Action**: User clicks the Project selector and types \"API\"\n  1319→- **Expected**: The selector filters to show only \"API Redesign\".\n  1320→\n  1321→#### Test: Project selector allows selecting a project\n  1322→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Project field is empty\n  1323→- **Action**: User clicks the Project selector and selects \"Mobile App\"\n  1324→- **Expected**: Project field shows \"Mobile App\".\n  1325→\n  1326→#### Test: Cycle dropdown shows team's available cycles\n  1327→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" selected. Team has cycles \"Sprint 10\" (active) and \"Sprint 11\" (upcoming).\n  1328→- **Action**: User clicks the Cycle dropdown\n  1329→- **Expected**: Dropdown shows \"Sprint 10\" and \"Sprint 11\". The active cycle is indicated.\n  1330→\n  1331→#### Test: Cycle dropdown allows selecting a cycle\n  1332→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Cycle field is empty\n  1333→- **Action**: User clicks the Cycle dropdown and selects \"Sprint 10\"\n  1334→- **Expected**: Cycle field shows \"Sprint 10\".\n  1335→\n  1336→#### Test: Cycle dropdown updates when team is changed\n  1337→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" selected showing its cycles\n  1338→- **Action**: User changes team to \"Design\" via the Team selector\n  1339→- **Expected**: The Cycle dropdown clears its selection and now shows \"Design\" team's cycles instead of \"Engineering\" cycles.\n  1340→\n  1341→#### Test: Due date picker allows selecting a date\n  1342→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Due date field is empty\n  1343→- **Action**: User clicks the Due date picker and selects a date (e.g., March 25, 2026)\n  1344→- **Expected**: Due date field shows \"Mar 25, 2026\".\n  1345→\n  1346→#### Test: Due date picker allows clearing the date\n  1347→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with due date \"Mar 25, 2026\" set\n  1348→- **Action**: User clicks the clear button on the Due date field\n  1349→- **Expected**: Due date field is empty again.\n  1350→\n  1351→#### Test: Parent issue selector is searchable\n  1352→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Issues \"ENG-1: Setup project\", \"ENG-2: Design database\" exist.\n  1353→- **Action**: User clicks the Parent issue selector and types \"Setup\"\n  1354→- **Expected**: The selector filters to show \"ENG-1: Setup project\".\n  1355→\n  1356→#### Test: Parent issue selector allows selecting a parent\n  1357→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open, Parent issue field is empty\n  1358→- **Action**: User clicks the Parent issue selector and selects \"ENG-1: Setup project\"\n  1359→- **Expected**: Parent issue field shows \"ENG-1: Setup project\".\n  1360→\n  1361→#### Test: Assignee selector can be used multiple times\n  1362→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with \"Alice Smith\" selected as assignee\n  1363→- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee selector, clears the selection, types \"Bob\", selects \"Bob Jones\", then repeats to select \"Carol Lee\"\n  1364→- **Expected**: Assignee field shows \"Carol Lee\" after the final selection. Each selection correctly replaces the previous one.\n  1365→\n  1366→#### Test: Labels selector can be used multiple times in sequence\n  1367→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with no labels selected\n  1368→- **Action**: User selects \"Bug\" label, then opens the selector again and adds \"Feature\", then opens again and removes \"Bug\" and adds \"Improvement\"\n  1369→- **Expected**: Labels field shows \"Feature\" and \"Improvement\" as colored badges.\n  1370→\n  1371→#### Test: Status dropdown can be changed multiple times\n  1372→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with Status \"Backlog\"\n  1373→- **Action**: User changes status to \"Todo\", then changes it to \"In Progress\", then back to \"Backlog\"\n  1374→- **Expected**: Status shows \"Backlog\" after the final change. Each intermediate state was correctly displayed.\n  1375→\n  1376→### CreateIssueActions\n  1377→\n  1378→#### Test: Create Issue button is visible and styled\n  1379→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1380→- **Expected**: A \"Create Issue\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal with primary styling (accent color background).\n  1381→\n  1382→#### Test: Cancel button is visible\n  1383→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1384→- **Expected**: A \"Cancel\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal alongside the \"Create Issue\" button.\n  1385→\n  1386→#### Test: Cancel button closes the modal\n  1387→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1388→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n  1389→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No issue is created. The user returns to the previous page view.\n  1390→\n  1391→#### Test: Cancel button discards form data\n  1392→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has entered title \"Draft issue\" and selected priority \"High\".\n  1393→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\", then opens the create issue modal again\n  1394→- **Expected**: The modal opens with all fields reset to defaults (empty title, Backlog status, No Priority). The previously entered data is not retained.\n  1395→\n  1396→#### Test: Create Issue button submits the form with all fields\n  1397→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has filled in: Title \"Implement OAuth\", Description \"Add OAuth support\", Status \"Todo\", Priority \"High\", Assignee \"Alice Smith\", Labels \"Feature\", Project \"API Redesign\", Cycle \"Sprint 10\", Due date \"Mar 25, 2026\".\n  1398→- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1399→- **Expected**: The issue is created with all specified field values. A brief confirmation showing the new issue identifier (e.g., \"ENG-43\") is displayed. The modal closes and the user is navigated to the issues list."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014vB59L6L4pzEX8iMoSPVUx","session_id":"76da8815-73a4-4291-afeb-dab9c3288c7d","uuid":"e44aac93-7958-4645-b3ed-331e94016e60"}
